  privacy_full_text:
    "<h3>1. Data Protection at a Glance</h3><p>The following information provides a simple overview of what happens to your personal data when you visit this website. Personal data is all data with which you can be personally identified.</p><h3>2. Controller (Verantwortlicher)</h3><p>The controller for data processing on this website is:<br>Jean Ari Jäger<br>Schillerstr. 6 B<br>76726 Germersheim<br>Deutschland<br>Email: contact@nhywyll.com</p><h3>3. Hosting</h3><p>This website is hosted by GitHub Pages (GitHub, Inc., USA). GitHub automatically collects and stores information in server log files. Data may be transferred to the USA in the process; GitHub is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. For further details, please refer to GitHub's privacy policy.</p><h3>4. Data Collection on this Website</h3><p><strong>Server Log Files:</strong> The provider of the pages automatically collects and stores information in so-called server log files, which your browser automatically transmits to us. These include: Browser type/version, OS, Referrer URL, Hostname, and Time of request. This data is not merged with other data sources. Basis: Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR.</p><h3>5. Contact by Email and Contact Form</h3><p>If you send me an email, I process your email address and the content of your message in order to answer your request. The contact form on this website does not send anything itself: it only opens your own email program with a pre-filled message, which you then send yourself. Emails are stored with my email provider Dynadot Inc. (USA). The legal basis is Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. b GDPR if your message concerns a contract or a request for one (e.g. a collaboration), otherwise my legitimate interest in answering your message (Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR). I delete your message once it has been dealt with, unless statutory retention obligations (e.g. for business letters) require otherwise.</p><h3>6. Google Analytics 4 (GA4)</h3><p>This website uses functions of the web analysis service Google Analytics (GA4). Provider is Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. GA4 uses cookies and similar technologies to analyze website usage. Data processing is based on your consent according to Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. a GDPR. You can withdraw your consent at any time via the cookie settings at the bottom of every page. GA4 does not store full IP addresses. Data may be transferred to Google LLC in the USA; Google is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. Event data (e.g. page views) is deleted automatically after 2 months, user data after 14 months; if you visit the website again, this period starts anew.</p><h3>7. Links to Other Platforms and Affiliate Links</h3><p>This website links to other platforms, for example Twitch, YouTube, TikTok, Bluesky, Discord and Ko-fi. Simply visiting this website does not transfer any data to these platforms; the Shorts thumbnails are stored on my own server. Only when you click a link do you leave this website, and the respective provider processes data under its own responsibility.</p><p>The links to Razer and Humble Bundle are affiliate links. If you buy something through them, I receive a commission; it does not cost you more. When clicked, the link passes through a tracking service of the partner or its affiliate network, which records that you came from this website and may set cookies for this. This only happens after your click and on the partner's pages. Please refer to their privacy policy there.</p><h3>8. Twitch Live Status</h3><p>To indicate whether a livestream is currently running, your browser calls the decapi.me interface when the page loads. Your IP address is transmitted to the provider of this interface in the process. No cookies are set and no personal profiles are created. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in displaying the current streaming status according to Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR.</p><h3>9. Your Rights</h3><p>You have the right at any time to information about your stored personal data (Art. 15 GDPR), to rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18) and data portability (Art. 20). You can withdraw any consent you have given at any time with effect for the future (Art. 7 Para. 3).</p><p><strong>Right to object (Art. 21 GDPR):</strong> Where I process data on the basis of my legitimate interest (Art. 6 Para. 1 lit. f GDPR), you can object at any time on grounds relating to your particular situation.</p><p>An email to <a href='mailto:contact@nhywyll.com' class='email-link'>contact@nhywyll.com</a> is enough for all of this.</p><h3>10. Local Storage</h3><p>We use the so-called local storage of your browser to store basic technical settings (such as your chosen language, dark/light mode and your decision in the cookie banner). This data remains locally on your device and is not transmitted to servers. It is essential for the correct display of the website.</p><h3>11. Supervisory Authority</h3><p>You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority. The competent authority is: Der Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit Rheinland-Pfalz (<a href='https://www.datenschutz.rlp.de' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' class='email-link'>https://www.datenschutz.rlp.de</a>).</p>",
